Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 09:39:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06878/11362] [outer-loop] ARC dc22 round-5: L4->L5, cracks the
 F-chute after 4 rounds

Round-5 claude-fable-5 attempt on dc22 solved L5, cracking the color-15/F
chute that resisted all four prior rounds. The missing piece was a HIDDEN
CONTROL, not a routing/timing fix: route the latched 8/12 assembly a
SECOND time so its color-12 slab creates a bridge to the previously
isolated solid F socket. Stepping onto that socket reveals a hidden F
button at (52,15) -- invisible until physically standing on the socket --
that swaps solidity between the vertical F chute and the horizontal F
bar. Descend the solid chute, use a B-shelf spanning both endpoints to
stay supported while the F button toggles back, then cross the now-
walkable horizontal bar to the B goal.

Source agent's own reproduction_verified is correctly false (gating the
322-action line would have exceeded budget), but the outer loop
independently verified it: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new
resolver priority branch, all 5 confirmed level=5, state=NOT_FINISHED.

L6 was scouted (a second hidden 8 control, a rotate-without-teleport 6
control, a shelf-cycling B control) but stayed condition-gated -- no win.

reproducible_total_levels 155 -> 156. arc_count_integrity_lint.py exit 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
